{
    "version": "4.74",
    "description": "Tftpd64: lightweight TFTP server and client, with DHCP, DNS, SNTP and Syslog servers; the usual tool to flash routers and boards from a bootloader over the network.",
    "homepage": "https://pjo2.github.io/tftpd64/",
    "license": {
        "identifier": "EUPL-1.2",
        "url": "https://github.com/PJO2/tftpd64/blob/HEAD/readme.txt"
    },
    "notes": [
        "Settings are kept in the persisted tftpd32.ini. Tftpd64 first looks for that file in %APPDATA%\\Tftpd64,",
        "%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Tftpd64, %ProgramData%\\Tftpd64 and similar folders: if an installer version left one",
        "there, that one wins. Set TFTPD32_INI_DIR to point it elsewhere.",
        "",
        "Allow it in Windows Firewall (private network) on the first start. For router recovery turn off the DHCP,",
        "DNS, SNTP and Syslog servers you don't need, give the PC the IP the bootloader expects (e.g. 192.168.0.66",
        "or 192.168.1.66 on TP-Link) and put the file under the name it asks for into the base directory."
    ],
    "architecture": {
        "64bit": {
